Apple-200688401.description:
Imagine what you could do here! At Apple, wonderful ideas have a way of becoming extraordinary products, services, and customer experiences very quickly. Bring passion and dedication to your job and there's no telling what you could accomplish.

At Apple, we don’t just build products — we create the kind of wonder that’s revolutionized entire industries. It’s the diversity of our people and their ideas that supports the innovation that runs through everything we do, from amazing technology to industry-leading environmental efforts. 

We invite you to join us on this venture and help us leave the world better than we found it!

In this highly hands-on role, you will enjoy the key decision-making combined with the on-site problem solving that comes with the responsibility for the quality of some of the best products in the world today. You will look after the development, the quality tools and systems for state of art designs in a cosmetically fast paced environment. Specific areas of responsibility include the following:

We are an equal opportunity employer and value diversity at our company. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status.

We will ensure that individuals with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodation to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and to receive other benefits and privileges of employment. Please contact us to request accommodation.

QUALITY PLANNING

Apply a deep understanding of quality control and manufacturing concepts to handle the development of specific Product Quality Plans (PQP) significant for program and commodity;

Evaluate and communicate the yield of new and existing processes;

Drive corrective actions transversally with team members;

Develop and implement innovative quality inspection tools;

Identify and direct studies to implement improvements in measuring method where appropriate;

Establish audit procedures appropriate to program and supplier to ensure Apple quality standards are applied;

Work with internal and external groups to ensure that accurate definition of quality expectations and that appropriate assurance techniques are used for the product. 

SUPPLIER QUALITY MANAGEMENT

Assess supplier production control and quality programs, identify shortfalls to expectation, and directly secure agreement for corrective actions to take;

Review PQP with supplier and other Apple functional groups to optimize supplier quality programs;

Evaluates supplier readiness and adequacy to PQP at all development and qualification stages;

Handle each supplier's performance through measurement of production line statistics, company inspections, and audits. Prepare summary of performance and communicate to appropriate management.

Apple-200688401.requirements:
Minimum qualifications / 最低资格
Master or Bachelor degree is required. Data and Engineering related or MBA will be a plus;

Experienced in the creation of quality plans, building test and measures, validating them, and make corrections;

Proficiency in Mandarin and English is required.

Preferred qualifications / 优先条件
Understand clearly how to apply problem solving within experiments design, root cause analysis and statistical process control;

Experienced a large number of cosmetic and dimensional issues in components and/or finished products in consumer electronic industry;

Experience in die castings, injection molding, tooling, jigs, fixtures, or quality manufacturing engineering in big numbers; experience in mechanical enclosures is a plus;

Knowledge on data mapping and analysis with statistical tools;

Experience in developing & application of quality solutions with machine learning algorithms;

Knowledge on quality and reliability, experience with GD&T and Failure Analysis;

Experience in coordinating with suppliers and contract manufacturers;

Good analytical skills, and capacity to reason on articulated issues.

